{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1009491-deaf-theurges-and-spirit-speech","id":1009491,"title":"Deaf Theurges and Spirit Speech","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-28T14:47:57-08:00","id":1009491,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Deaf Theurges and Spirit Speech","content":"Could a deaf Theurge still learn the gift Spirit Speech?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":".  Werewolf powers are called gifts not charms. 11-28-2016, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T16:01:25-08:00","id":1009527,"title":"","content":"It's supposed to be a kind of empathic communication, so I would say yes. Spirits aren't physical so they are not bound by the rules of the physical world - their speech is not actual sound although it is interpreted to be so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T16:02:50-08:00","id":1009528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1009491-deaf-theurges-and-spirit-speech?p=1009527#post1009527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's supposed to be a kind of empathic communication, so I would say yes. Spirits aren't physical so they are not bound by the rules of the physical world - their speech is not actual sound although it is interpreted to be so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreeing with this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T16:47:07-08:00","id":1009546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1009491-deaf-theurges-and-spirit-speech?p=1009527#post1009527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's supposed to be a kind of empathic communication, so I would say yes. Spirits aren't physical so they are not bound by the rules of the physical world - their speech is not actual sound although it is interpreted to be so.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awesome. I'll describe it as the Theurge interpreting the mannerisms and movements of the spirit. The spirit is not using sign language, but the if the Theurge can see the spirit move, they know what the spirit is trying to communicate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T17:26:38-08:00","id":1009561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1009491-deaf-theurges-and-spirit-speech?p=1009546#post1009546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Awesome. I'll describe it as the Theurge interpreting the mannerisms and movements of the spirit. The spirit is not using sign language, but the if the Theurge can see the spirit move, they know what the spirit is trying to communicate.</div> </div> </div> </div>And keep in mind the nature of the spirit. A water spirit might bubble or crest, while a wind spirit might howl and/or move. The type of spirit has always mattered a lot in how they communicate in games I've ran or played. Some spirits might be more difficult to understand than others, but with effort the Gift should work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T17:39:44-08:00","id":1009565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1009491-deaf-theurges-and-spirit-speech?p=1009561#post1009561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And keep in mind the nature of the spirit. A water spirit might bubble or crest, while a wind spirit might howl and/or move. The type of spirit has always mattered a lot in how they communicate in games I've ran or played. Some spirits might be more difficult to understand than others, but with effort the Gift should work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. I could see the deaf Theurge communicate with the Wind Spirit by watching the leaves in the Wind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T03:00:45-08:00","id":1010563,"title":"","content":"Most spirits don't really speak human languages. Pain spirits speak in pain and the desires to inflict and experience such. Wind spirits speak in gusts and breezes. Axiom spirits could communicate only through complex mathematical expressions. Spirit Speech just allows you to comprehend them and for them to comprehend you. It's not really &quot;speech&quot; per se.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T22:22:26-08:00","id":1015163,"title":"","content":"A good point bring up is that the Mute flaw will prevent you from speaking in Spirit Tongue though, so there is grounds that a verbal component is pretty much universally necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12487-cantankerous-bees","name":"Cantankerous Bees","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T19:57:14-08:00","id":1015495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cantankerous Bees</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1009491-deaf-theurges-and-spirit-speech?p=1015163#post1015163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A good point bring up is that the Mute flaw will prevent you from speaking in Spirit Tongue though, so there is grounds that a verbal component is pretty much universally necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am going to lean on the rules and say taking the Deaf flaw doesn't automatically mean you must take the Mute flaw. Some deaf people can speak English and read lips. I already was planning on taking English as a Language merit (ASL would be native) for the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T22:37:38-08:00","id":1015552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1009491-deaf-theurges-and-spirit-speech?p=1015495#post1015495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am going to lean on the rules and say taking the Deaf flaw doesn't automatically mean you must take the Mute flaw. Some deaf people can speak English and read lips. I already was planning on taking English as a Language merit (ASL would be native) for the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't saying that you need to take the mute flaw alongside being deaf, I was just pointing out that spirit speech isn't necessarily just some spiritual resonance kind of thing.<br /> <br /> There is some sort of language and verbal component to it so your ability to understand what a spirit trying to communicate to you is going to be pretty hampered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12487-cantankerous-bees","name":"Cantankerous Bees","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T14:03:04-08:00","id":1015831,"title":"","content":"Mute negating your ability to speak with Spirit Speech doesn't mean the Spirit needs to speak. Speech is how humans communicate, so an inability to do that may mean Spirit Speech is unable to &quot;translate&quot; your speech to the spirit. But the Spirit should still be able to communicate with you.<br /> <br /> The Mute Flaw also states that you can't even communicate with the lupine language (which they say requires vocalizations as well as body language). So it's very strict. At the same time, later they say that if people know the same sign language and such, they can communicate. As well as through body language or writing. I would say a Mute character who knows Sign Language, and therefore a way to communicate his thoughts, and can do that, then Spirit Speech would translate that to the spirit.<br /> <br /> So we can see Spirit Speech not as its own separate form of communication, but a way to translate the normal communication done in the Realm and the way the Spirits communicate between each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}